From: FormalSnake <kyaniserni@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:56:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/30] gpui_windows: leave a caption press to DefWindowProc

A press on a drag area belongs to DefWindowProc: its move loop, Snap, and maximize on double
click. Dispatched as a mouse down, the element that owns the area takes it, and the window
never moves.
---
 crates/gpui_windows/src/events.rs | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/gpui_windows/src/events.rs b/crates/gpui_windows/src/events.rs
index 465b6b14a6..0c8b852337 100644
--- a/crates/gpui_windows/src/events.rs
+++ b/crates/gpui_windows/src/events.rs
@@ -1083,6 +1083,12 @@ impl WindowsWindowInner {
         wparam: WPARAM,
         lparam: LPARAM,
     ) -> Option<isize> {
+        // A press on a drag area belongs to `DefWindowProc`: its move loop, Snap, and maximize
+        // on double click. Dispatched, the element that owns the area takes it (it starts its
+        // own move on other platforms), and the window never moves.
+        if wparam.0 as u32 == HTCAPTION {
+            return None;
+        }
         if let Some(mut func) = self.state.callbacks.input.take() {
             let scale_factor = self.state.scale_factor.get();
             let mut cursor_point = POINT {
